{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pv75GYpF85pQHYkVVxuvhY","type":"tool_result","content":"225\t      # Step: Hook executable bits (.sh + active Python hooks)\n226\t      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n227\t      - name: Hook and script executable bits\n228\t        run: |\n229\t          set -euo pipefail\n230\t          MISSING=\"\"\n231\t          # All .sh files under scripts/ and hooks/ (includes legacy for\n232\t          # completeness — fallback scripts should still be executable).\n233\t          while IFS= read -r -d '' script; do\n234\t            if [ ! -x \"$script\" ]; then\n235\t              MISSING=\"$MISSING $script\"\n236\t            fi\n237\t          done < <(find .claude/scripts .claude/hooks -name '*.sh' -print0 2>/dev/null)\n238\t          # Active Python hooks (not _lib or tests — those are libraries)\n239\t          for py in .claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py .claude/hooks/audit_log.py .claude/hooks/check_bash_safety.py .claude/hooks/check_plan_edit.py; do\n240\t            if [ -f \"$py\" ] && [ ! -x \"$py\" ]; then\n241\t              MISSING=\"$MISSING $py\"\n242\t            fi\n243\t          done\n244\t          if [ -n \"$MISSING\" ]; then\n245\t            echo \"❌ The following files are not executable:\"\n246\t            for m in $MISSING; do echo \"  - $m\"; done\n247\t            echo \"\"\n248\t            echo \"Run: chmod +x <file>\"\n249\t            exit 1\n250\t          fi\n251\t          echo \"✓ All active hooks/scripts are executable\"\n252\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e86bd57-c683-4f2c-b9eb-449a331f3f20","uuid":"d0373f66-d477-443a-b82f-9be950fb9a2e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:03:54.905Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/templates/.github/workflows/validate.yml.template","content":"      # Step: Hook executable bits (.sh + active Python hooks)\n      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n      - name: Hook and script executable bits\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          MISSING=\"\"\n          # All .sh files under scripts/ and hooks/ (includes legacy for\n          # completeness — fallback scripts should still be executable).\n          while IFS= read -r -d '' script; do\n            if [ ! -x \"$script\" ]; then\n              MISSING=\"$MISSING $script\"\n            fi\n          done < <(find .claude/scripts .claude/hooks -name '*.sh' -print0 2>/dev/null)\n          # Active Python hooks (not _lib or tests — those are libraries)\n          for py in .claude/hooks/check_agent_spawn.py .claude/hooks/audit_log.py .claude/hooks/check_bash_safety.py .claude/hooks/check_plan_edit.py; do\n            if [ -f \"$py\" ] && [ ! -x \"$py\" ]; then\n              MISSING=\"$MISSING $py\"\n            fi\n          done\n          if [ -n \"$MISSING\" ]; then\n            echo \"❌ The following files are not executable:\"\n            for m in $MISSING; do echo \"  - $m\"; done\n            echo \"\"\n            echo \"Run: chmod +x <file>\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          echo \"✓ All active hooks/scripts are executable\"\n","numLines":28,"startLine":225,"totalLines":252}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pv75GYpF85pQHYkVVxuvhY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1NK4apbPsByKWwUkpHh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016e4ekaz1bg2Gvy2GYZAqS9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":75,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5867,"cache_read_input_tokens":152999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5867},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e86bd57-c683-4f2c-b9eb-449a331f3f20","uuid":"3f899b4d-817f-4e4d-a963-f651c168dace","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:03:56.636Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1NK4Kw7mWBw22jJK4CG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016e4ekaz1bg2Gvy2GYZAqS9":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":75,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016e4ekaz1bg2Gvy2GYZAqS9","type":"tool_result","content":"75\thas both: the indirect-execution guard on by default, and the model checks\n76\tand Codex pin above. Plan an upgrade from v1.4.2 as you would plan a MINOR\n77\tone.\n78\t\n79\t### Added — a Bash guard against indirect execution, on by default (PLAN-195, ADR-201)\n80\t\n81\t- After its existing checks, `check_bash_safety.py` runs one bounded scan\n82\t  (`_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py`). The scan looks for `rm -rf`,\n83\t  `git reset --hard` or a forced `git push` reached indirectly:\n84\t  - inside `sh -c`, `eval` or a here-doc;\n85\t  - behind a known launcher;\n86\t  - through a computed command name;\n87\t  - in a program fed by a pipe, a redirect, a descriptor or a process\n88\t    substitution.\n89\t- It also blocks a computed write when it resolves the target from the\n90\t  command text to a canonical path.\n91\t- It only adds blocks; an earlier BLOCK stays BLOCK. Its reason codes are\n92\t  `bash_indirect_*` and `bash_computed_canonical_target`.\n93\t- It fails closed on a recognized shell body it cannot parse, and at its\n94\t  depth, size and word limits.\n95\t- Two switches control it. Both are on unless set to `0` in the\n96\t  environment Claude Code starts with:\n97\t  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0` turns off the scan;\n98\t  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0` turns off only the computed-verb and\n99\t    opaque-feeder forms.\n100\t- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n101\t  session and switch.\n102\t\n103\t### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n104\t\n105\t- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n106\t  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n107\t  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n108\t- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n109\t\n110\t### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n111\t\n112\t- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n113\t  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n114\t  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n115\t  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n116\t  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n117\t  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n118\t- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n119\t  `_lib` entry except the test harness. On the merge of pull request #7,\n120\t  the Smoke Install push run passed; a manually dispatched run was\n121\t  cancelled.\n122\t- If you patched a hook by hand, the entry point no longer holds the logic.\n123\t  Re-apply the patch to the module.\n124\t- The compatibility evidence is the test suites. No differential replay\n125\t  against the code before the split is claimed.\n126\t\n127\t### Changed — a registered hook leaves its spool work pending at exit (ADR-055-AMEND-4, partial)\n128\t\n129\t- `_python-hook.sh` exports `CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1`. A hook that runs\n130\t  with it does not drain its audit spool at exit or on a signal. It leaves\n131\t  an `exit_deadline_skip` breadcrumb instead, and its events wait in the\n132\t  spool for a later drain, so they can reach the log later.\n133\t- This removes the forced exit drain that could outlast a hook's timeout.\n134\t- ADR-055-AMEND-4 is `ACCEPTED` with its implementation `PARTIAL`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e86bd57-c683-4f2c-b9eb-449a331f3f20","uuid":"a6ebd090-4785-4bab-bc3b-a82fdd0f4cc3","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:03:56.653Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"has both: the indirect-execution guard on by default, and the model checks\nand Codex pin above. Plan an upgrade from v1.4.2 as you would plan a MINOR\none.\n\n### Added — a Bash guard against indirect execution, on by default (PLAN-195, ADR-201)\n\n- After its existing checks, `check_bash_safety.py` runs one bounded scan\n  (`_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py`). The scan looks for `rm -rf`,\n  `git reset --hard` or a forced `git push` reached indirectly:\n  - inside `sh -c`, `eval` or a here-doc;\n  - behind a known launcher;\n  - through a computed command name;\n  - in a program fed by a pipe, a redirect, a descriptor or a process\n    substitution.\n- It also blocks a computed write when it resolves the target from the\n  command text to a canonical path.\n- It only adds blocks; an earlier BLOCK stays BLOCK. Its reason codes are\n  `bash_indirect_*` and `bash_computed_canonical_target`.\n- It fails closed on a recognized shell body it cannot parse, and at its\n  depth, size and word limits.\n- Two switches control it. Both are on unless set to `0` in the\n  environment Claude Code starts with:\n  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0` turns off the scan;\n  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0` turns off only the computed-verb and\n    opaque-feeder forms.\n- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n  session and switch.\n\n### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n\n- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n\n### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n\n- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n  `_lib` entry except the test harness. On the merge of pull request #7,\n  the Smoke Install push run passed; a manually dispatched run was\n  cancelled.\n- If you patched a hook by hand, the entry point no longer holds the logic.\n  Re-apply the patch to the module.\n- The compatibility evidence is the test suites. No differential replay\n  against the code before the split is claimed.\n\n### Changed — a registered hook leaves its spool work pending at exit (ADR-055-AMEND-4, partial)\n\n- `_python-hook.sh` exports `CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1`. A hook that runs\n  with it does not drain its audit spool at exit or on a signal. It leaves\n  an `exit_deadline_skip` breadcrumb instead, and its events wait in the\n  spool for a later drain, so they can reach the log later.\n- This removes the forced exit drain that could outlast a hook's timeout.\n- ADR-055-AMEND-4 is `ACCEPTED` with its implementation `PARTIAL`","numLines":60,"startLine":75,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016e4ekaz1bg2Gvy2GYZAqS9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
